SDL2 Metal renderer: texture updates through a pool of upload buffers instead of a staging texture each

After a texture's first upload, SDL 2.32's Metal renderer copies every update into a new staging texture and blits
that over (its own TODO asks for a pool). A video player updates two or three planes per frame; with StrixArc's
Metal plugin each new texture is a Vulkan image with GPU memory allocated, mapped and freed through the kext, and the
upload into it a GPU copy waited on - about a fifth of a core at 4K 30 fps (round 56's profile). Updates now memcpy
into a shared MTLBuffer and blit buffer -> texture in the same command buffer; the buffer goes back to the pool when
that command buffer completes (best fit, at most 8 kept). Formats other than 8/16-bit R/RG/RGBA keep the old path.

